# Content Calendar

> Your dated editorial plan. Derived from `references/positioning.md` (Weekly content calendar
> themes + Focus areas + Content pillars). Filled during `/onboard` (the storytelling-strategist
> sequence) and editable anytime. `/post` reads the row for the target DATE to build the post brief;
> `/start-day` surfaces today's planned post.
>
> **Theme + Objective are FIXED by weekday** — they live once in the legend below (and the master
> copy in `positioning.md → Weekly content calendar`), so the table doesn't repeat them per row.
> Each table row carries only what varies: the **Pillar focus** (this month's facet of the day's
> pillar) and the specific **Topic / Angle**. `/post` composes the row into this exact brief:
>
> > I want to talk about **{Pillar focus}** on a **{Day}** with the theme (**{Theme}**).
> > Reason for this theme is because **{Objective}**.
> > Give me a post on **{Topic / Angle}** in this content pillar.
>
> Theme + Objective are looked up by weekday from the legend; only Pillar focus + Topic come from
> the row. Coaching = Mode 1; financial topics flip to Mode 2 (concept-only).

## How this calendar is built (structure to keep)

Two layers fix the editorial rhythm so every row is purposeful, not random:

1. **Weekday themes (the horizontal rhythm) — FIXED in the legend / `positioning.md`.** Each weekday
   owns one Theme + Objective (e.g. Mon empowering/mindset · Tue personal story · Wed expertise/how-to
   · Thu authority/contrarian · Fri growth/reflection). The same five recur every week, so they are
   stored ONCE in the legend, not retyped per row. To change a Theme or Objective, amend
   `positioning.md` and the legend, not the table.

2. **Monthly themes (the vertical arc) — one campaign idea per month.** Give each month a single
   umbrella theme so the year tells a story instead of looping. The **Pillar focus** column carries
   each weekday's facet of that month's theme. Example arc (replace with your own):
   `Month 1 = the core problem you solve · Month 2 = the system/method · Month 3 = the mindset shift ·
   Month 4 = the transition it requires · Month 5 = proof + objections · Month 6 = vision + reflection`.
   List your monthly themes above the table so the arc is visible at a glance.

The grid is **5 posts/week, Mon–Fri** (add Sun if your weekly structure includes it). Skip the dates
already past when you generate, and start the table from the next upcoming weekday. Leave a few
**`(open)`** slots near the end of the horizon rather than over-planning months out.

## Standard weekday themes (the legend — fixed)

> Mirror of `positioning.md → Weekly content calendar`. `/start-day` and `/post` read Theme +
> Objective from here by weekday.

| Day | Theme | Objective |
|-----|-------|-----------|
| Mon | [ Mon theme ] | [ Mon objective ] |
| Tue | [ Tue theme ] | [ Tue objective ] |
| Wed | [ Wed theme ] | [ Wed objective ] |
| Thu | [ Thu theme ] | [ Thu objective ] |
| Fri | [ Fri theme ] | [ Fri objective ] |

## Monthly themes (the arc — fill your own)

> [ Month 1 = theme · Month 2 = theme · Month 3 = theme · … ] — one umbrella idea per month; every
> row that month is a facet of it (carried in the Pillar focus column).

| Date | Day | Pillar focus | Topic / Angle | Status |
|------|-----|--------------|---------------|--------|
| [ YYYY-MM-DD ] | [ Mon ] | [ this month's facet of the Mon pillar ] | [ the specific topic/angle for this date ] | [ planned / drafted / published ] |
| [ YYYY-MM-DD ] | [ Tue ] | [ this month's facet ] | [ topic/angle ] | [ planned ] |
| [ YYYY-MM-DD ] | [ Wed ] | [ this month's facet ] | [ topic/angle — Mode 2 concept-only if financial ] | [ planned ] |
| [ YYYY-MM-DD ] | [ Thu ] | [ this month's facet ] | [ topic/angle ] | [ planned ] |
| [ YYYY-MM-DD ] | [ Fri ] | [ this month's facet ] | [ topic/angle ] | [ planned ] |
| … | … | … | … | … |
| [ YYYY-MM-DD ] | [ Mon ] | [ (open) ] | [ open slot — capture a fresh angle near the horizon ] | [ planned ] |
